"""
tsmctl - a read-only, kubectl-style CLI for TradeSkillMaster (TSM) data.

tsmctl reads the files TSM leaves on disk and never writes to them:

  * WTF/Account/<account>/SavedVariables/TradeSkillMaster.lua
      accounting ledgers (sales, buys, income, expenses, expired, cancelled),
      per-character gold and gold logs, bag/bank/mail/auction/warbank/guild
      inventory, TSM groups, and the TSM item-info cache (names, quality,
      vendor prices).
  * Interface/AddOns/TradeSkillMaster_AppHelper/AppData.lua
      the AuctionDB market data the TSM desktop app downloads (realm min
      buyout, market value, historical; region market, sale avg, sale rate,
      sold per day).

The WoW install can be local, or on another machine reached over ssh. Remote
data is pulled with `find` and `tar c` only (read-only on the remote) into a
local cache, and only re-copied when a file's mtime or size changes.

Everything prints to stdout. Nothing is written anywhere unless --save is
given, which writes an org-mode report into the notes repo (or a given path).

Only the Python standard library is used.
"""

